teather (0.1.0-9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Connect as the only internet path when the host has no other link (D-025).
    preflight no longer refuses with no-default / resolver-unavailable. With
    automatic failover armed, Teather comes up as the primary path and relies on
    tun2proxy virtual DNS plus the phone-side sentinel for resolution; if
    failover is off and there is no other internet, connect refuses and asks you
    to run 'teather failover on'. Fallback to Wi-Fi/Ethernet when one appears is
    unchanged (worse route metric, additive DNS).

