teather (0.1.0-6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * UDP support (D-024). tun2proxy is now built with its `udpgw` feature and run
    with `--udpgw-server`; the phone's new UdpGatewayServer terminates the
    framed-datagram stream over the existing SOCKS connection and forwards each
    datagram on the selected upstream. No second ADB forward, no VpnService, no
    packet stack on the phone. IPv6 UDP is still refused. NOTE: this package
    requires the tun2proxy binary rebuilt with `--features udpgw`.
  * `teather upstream` now rebinds the phone's relay upstream with no teardown,
    using the Android app's new ACTION_RECONFIGURE (versionCode 3, 0.1.0-p1.1).
    The SOCKS listener, teather0, the tunnel, routes, and DNS all stay up and
    established sessions keep their transport, so no connection sees a gap.
  * The Android launcher icon now matches the Linux client artwork, and the
    app's on-screen description no longer carries stale "P0 / TCP CONNECT only"
    wording.

 -- Teather Project <noreply@example.invalid>  Sat, 30 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000

